    <item>
      <title>6. Notes for Tab Bar Controller</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/docs/04-advanced-ui-components/useful-ui-elements/5.-tab-bar-controller/5.6.-notes-for-tab-bar-controller/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/04-advanced-ui-components/useful-ui-elements/5.-tab-bar-controller/5.6.-notes-for-tab-bar-controller/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;56-notes-for-tab-bar-controller&#34;&gt;5.6. Notes for Tab Bar Controller&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#56-notes-for-tab-bar-controller&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tab Bar Controller is a powerful tool.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Each tab has its own Navigation Controller. So, you can build a separate tree of screens for each tab with its navigation.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So, each tab can potentially work like a separate multiscreen app module.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can play around with the UI style elements of the tab bar items to design them as you like.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
